        "file": "ventures/sql-migration-lock-check/engine.mjs",
        "issue": "lock_timeout was a one-way latch: once any SET lock_timeout appeared, every later exclusive-lock statement read as protected, even after SET lock_timeout = 0 / TO DEFAULT / RESET lock_timeout / RESET ALL, after the COMMIT that ended a SET LOCAL, or after a ROLLBACK that undid the SET. So a migration that set a timeout for one block and dropped it got a clean no-lock-timeout result on the statements that could take the table down. Reproduced with 3 failing tests (engine.test.mjs, 'turning lock_timeout off again...', 'SET LOCAL lock_timeout stops applying...', 'ROLLBACK undoes...'); fixed by tracking session, local and at-BEGIN values.",
